data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1793, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "a4eae622-22b7-4cf4-b41a-05cd3de7def1", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "agent", "position": 1793, "revision": 1793, "parent_tool_use_id": "call_e7e057924f3a40a980c8d2d2", "agent_call_id": "b3ffe44d-6be1-4f63-8a26-cdae502c8404", "data": {"status": "running", "agent_type": "general-purpose", "sdk_agent_id": "a85d91b2fb09d939a", "task": "You are a general-purpose sub-agent working on a scientific data analysis task. Your job is to independently recompute angular coefficient statistics from raw TSV data and save results to a specific output path.\n\n**Task:** Recompute Legendre angular coefficient F20 evolution from raw data, writing your own code from scratch (do NOT read or copy any existing analysis scripts). Save results to `[workspace]`.\n\n**Data file:** `[workspace]`\n\n**Data format:** Long-format TSV with columns: dataset_path, index_0, index_1, value. \n- Each energy block has a dataset_path like \"CoefLeg_22.5eV\", \"CoefLeg_23.25eV\", etc.\n- index_0 = 0 means order=0 coefficients; other values mean different orders.\n- The 13 measured energies are: 22.5, 23.25, 24.8, 26.35, 27.9, 29.45, 31.0, 32.55, 34.1, 35.65, 37.2, 38.75, 48.4 eV.\n- You need to extract F20 values at both order=0 and order=1 across all 13 energies.\n\n**What to compute and save as JSON:**\n```json\n{\n  \"analysis\": \"B - Angular Coefficient F20 Evolution (Independent Rebuild)\",\n  \"num_energy_levels\": 13,\n  \"energy_range_eV\": [22.5, 48.4],\n  \"f20_order0\": {\n    \"values\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>}, ...],\n    \"sequence\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"first_differences\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"local_extrema\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>, \"type\": \"min\"/\"max\"}, ...],\n    \"is_monotonic\": <bool>,\n    \"polynomial_fits\": {\"degree_3\": {\"coefficients\": [<float>,...], \"r_squared\": <float>}}\n  },\n  \"f20_order1\": {\n    \"values\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>}, ...],\n    \"sequence\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"sign_changes\": <int>,\n    \"sign_change_energies\": []\n  },\n  \"all_order0_coeffs\": { \"<energy>\": { \"<index_1>\": <value>, ... }, ... },\n  \"all_order1_coeffs\": { \"<energy>\": { \"<index_1>\": <value>, ... }, ... }\n}\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Write your OWN code. Do not read any existing analysis scripts.\n- Use pandas/numpy/scipy only.\n- Be careful with column indexing — inspect the actual data structure first.\n- Save ONLY to the reproduce_test/output path specified above.\n- Print summary stats to stdout so I can verify.", "text": "", "error_code": null}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:58:55.867396+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:58:55.867404+00:00"}}

id: 1796
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1796, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "cb4bc20d-14d2-4278-bc48-6ff9d1b3dceb", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "tool", "position": 1789, "revision": 1796, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Agent", "input": "{\"description\": \"Angular coeff independent rebuild\", \"prompt\": \"You are a general-purpose sub-agent working on a scientific data analysis task. Your job is to independently recompute angular coefficient statistics from raw TSV data and save results to a specific output path.\\n\\n**Task:** Recompute Legendre angular coefficient F20 evolution from raw data, writing your own code from scratch (do NOT read or copy any existing analysis scripts). Save results to `[workspace]`.\\n\\n**Data file:** `[workspace]`\\n\\n**Data format:** Long-format TSV with columns: dataset_path, index_0, index_1, value. \\n- Each energy block has a dataset_path like \\\"CoefLeg_22.5eV\\\", \\\"CoefLeg_23.25eV\\\", etc.\\n- index_0 = 0 means order=0 coefficients; other values mean different orders.\\n- The 13 measured energies are: 22.5, 23.25, 24.8, 26.35, 27.9, 29.45, 31.0, 32.55, 34.1, 35.65, 37.2, 38.75, 48.4 eV.\\n- You need to extract F20 values at both order=0 and order=1 across all 13 energies.\\n\\n**What to compute and save as JSON:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": \\\"B - Angular Coefficient F20 Evolution (Independent Rebuild)\\\",\\n  \\\"num_energy_levels\\\": 13,\\n  \\\"energy_range_eV\\\": [22.5, 48.4],\\n  \\\"f20_order0\\\": {\\n    \\\"values\\\": [{\\\"energy_eV\\\": <float>, \\\"F20_value\\\": <float>}, ...],\\n    \\\"sequence\\\": [<float>, ...],\\n    \\\"first_differences\\\": [<float>, ...],\\n    \\\"local_extrema\\\": [{\\\"energy_eV\\\": <float>, \\\"F20_value\\\": <float>, \\\"type\\\": \\\"min\\\"/\\\"max\\\"}, ...],\\n    \\\"is_monotonic\\\": <bool>,\\n    \\\"polynomial_fits\\\": {\\\"degree_3\\\": {\\\"coefficients\\\": [<float>,...], \\\"r_squared\\\": <float>}}\\n  },\\n  \\\"f20_order1\\\": {\\n    \\\"values\\\": [{\\\"energy_eV\\\": <float>, \\\"F20_value\\\": <float>}, ...],\\n    \\\"sequence\\\": [<float>, ...],\\n    \\\"sign_changes\\\": <int>,\\n    \\\"sign_change_energies\\\": []\\n  },\\n  \\\"all_order0_coeffs\\\": { \\\"<energy>\\\": { \\\"<index_1>\\\": <value>, ... }, ... },\\n  \\\"all_order1_coeffs\\\": { \\\"<energy>\\\": { \\\"<index_1>\\\": <value>, ... }, ... }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Important:** \\n- Write your OWN code. Do not read any existing analysis scripts.\\n- Use pandas/numpy/scipy only.\\n- Be careful with column indexing — inspect the actual data structure first.\\n- Save ONLY to the reproduce_test/output path specified above.\\n- Print summary stats to stdout so I can verify.\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\", \"run_in_background\": false}", "output": "[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\\nagentId: a85d91b2fb09d939a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a85d91b2fb09d939a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\\noutput_file: [workspace] NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification.\"}]", "status": "completed", "is_async": true, "tool_use_id": "call_e7e057924f3a40a980c8d2d2"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:58:52.406128+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:58:55.913507+00:00"}}

