id: 1906
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1906, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "51314e01-1d7d-40b8-93f1-7775005a8727", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "text", "position": 1906, "revision": 1906, "parent_tool_use_id": "call_e7e057924f3a40a980c8d2d2", "agent_call_id": "b3ffe44d-6be1-4f63-8a26-cdae502c8404", "data": {"text": "The existing output is clearly wrong - it has 9 energy levels (0-8) instead of 13, and the F20 values are jumbled. The task says to independently recompute from scratch. Let me look at what \"F20\" means in this context. In Legendre polynomial notation, F_lm typically refers to coefficient l,m. Given the data only goes up to index_1=10, F20 likely means `index_1=2` (the l=2 Legendre coefficient). Let me verify by checking the existing analysis scripts for clues.\n\n"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:59:36.532100+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:59:36.532112+00:00"}}

