data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 2025, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "2c64e1dd-ae4f-4cf5-b975-b3418da4d200", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "text", "position": 2021, "revision": 2025, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Now I see the full picture. The authoritative `output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json` is a **stale/incorrect file** — it has `num_energy_levels: 9`, energy range `[0, 8]`, and all values have wrong energy labels (0.0, 1.0, 2.0... instead of actual energies). This was the original sub-agent output from Round 2 that had the column-parsing bug.\n\nMy direct computation produced the **correct** F20 values at the correct energies. The authoritative file is itself wrong. Let me verify this understanding by checking what the comparison actually showed in v2:\n\n"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T10:02:09.879743+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T10:02:11.344981+00:00"}}

