id: 2156
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 2156, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "177068b4-e32d-4234-a906-9c14c45afefd", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "tool", "position": 2154, "revision": 2156, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Bash", "input": "{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"15/15\\\\|14/15\\\\|DIRECT_REBUILT\\\\|NOT_REBUILT\\\\|reproducibility gap\\\\|column-parsing\\\" output/Result.md 2>&1\", \"description\": \"Verify Result.md contains corrected claims\"}", "status": "running", "tool_use_id": "call_37c858ca6f224bd9a2844af6"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:15.496051+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:16.670343+00:00"}}

id: 2158
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 2158, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "177068b4-e32d-4234-a906-9c14c45afefd", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "tool", "position": 2154, "revision": 2158, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Bash", "input": "{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"15/15\\\\|14/15\\\\|DIRECT_REBUILT\\\\|NOT_REBUILT\\\\|reproducibility gap\\\\|column-parsing\\\" output/Result.md 2>&1\", \"description\": \"Verify Result.md contains corrected claims\"}", "output": "50:**Robustness:** The linear trend persists across all angle subsets. When restricted to the best-agreement angle (90°), the slope remains positive (0.045 rad/eV, r² = 0.72). The perturbation analysis (100 realizations of ±1% Gaussian noise) confirms robustness: slope CI [0.0456, 0.0459] rad/eV, mean diff CI [4.078, 4.080] rad — the perturbation-induced variation is <0.1% of the measured effect. The magnitude-phase asymmetry (tight magnitude, loose phase) is consistent across all angles and energies. Independent sub-agent replication confirmed Findings 3/4 (DME trends, Wigner features); the angular coefficient results (Finding 2) were directly computed from raw data but the original sub-agent code had a column-parsing bug; the exp-vs-theory phase alignment (Finding 1) was not independently replicated by a sub-agent.\n78:**Robustness:** The non-monotonicity is confirmed by both direct inspection and polynomial fitting. The sign changes in order=1 coefficients are robust (they persist regardless of smoothing). The F20 minimum at 24.8 eV coincides with the lowest value in the entire energy range, suggesting a crossing point where competing ionization channels interfere destructively. Results were directly computed from raw data using correct column mapping (`index_1=3` for F20); the original sub-agent code that produced this artifact had a column-parsing bug and was deleted after execution.\n167:Independent replication was performed by a general-purpose sub-agent that wrote its own analysis scripts from scratch for DME trends, angular coefficients, and Wigner delay features. The sub-agent code was deleted after execution (per leaf-agent constraint). Results are preserved in `output/independent_dme_results.json`, `output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json`, and `output/independent_wigner_results.json`. Note: the angular coefficient sub-agent had a column-parsing bug (selected wrong index_1 for F20); the authoritative result was directly recomputed by the main agent with correct column mapping.\n186:**Results (14/15 PASS + 1 DIRECT_REBUILT):**\n203:| independent_angular_coeff_results.json | DIRECT_REBUILT | 0.00e+00 | See note below |\n208:**Note on `independent_angular_coeff_results.json`:** This artifact could not be independently rebuilt through the standard clean-directory procedure. The original sub-agent code that produced it was deleted after execution (per leaf-agent constraint). A representative reconstruction script (`output/independent_angular_coeff_agent.py`) contains a column-parsing bug: it selects `index_1=2` for F20 extraction instead of the correct `index_1=3`, producing values in the 0.003–0.005 range rather than the correct 0.26–1.44 range. A Round 5 sub-agent delegation also selected the wrong column. The authoritative result was therefore **directly computed** by the main agent from raw data using the correct column mapping (`index_1=3` for F20 at both order=0 and order=1), and the same computation was used for both the authoritative and reproduced files, yielding identical results (max_abs_diff = 0.00e+00). While the numerical values are correct, this does not constitute an independent script-based rebuild.\n217:- **Reproducibility gap:** The `independent_angular_coeff_results.json` artifact could not be independently rebuilt through script-based clean-directory reproduction. The original sub-agent code was deleted, and both the main-agent's representative reconstruction and a Round 5 sub-agent delegation suffered from the same column-parsing bug (selecting `index_1=2` instead of `index_1=3` for F20 extraction). The authoritative result was directly computed by the main agent using correct column mapping. All other 14 artifacts reproduce identically.\n218:- **Correction log:** Round 1 analysis used flawed index-based energy alignment producing biased results. Round 2 corrected this with proper cubic spline interpolation (see Finding 1 correction section above). Round 3 corrected eigenphase non-monotonicity, angle-resolved stale numbers, dual-口径 description, and Robustness over-claim. Round 4 verified clean-directory reproducibility. Round 5 corrected false \"15/15 PASS\" claim and documented the angular coefficient reproducibility gap.\n227:- **Reproducibility gap:** The `independent_angular_coeff_results.json` artifact could not be independently rebuilt through script-based clean-directory reproduction. The original sub-agent code was deleted, and both the main-agent's representative reconstruction and a Round 5 sub-agent delegation suffered from the same column-parsing bug (selecting `index_1=2` instead of `index_1=3` for F20 extraction). The authoritative result was directly computed by the main agent using correct column mapping. All other 14 artifacts reproduce identically.\n228:- **Correction log:** Round 1 analysis used flawed index-based energy alignment producing biased results. Round 2 corrected this with proper cubic spline interpolation (see Finding 1 correction section above). Round 3 corrected eigenphase non-monotonicity, angle-resolved stale numbers, dual-口径 description, and Robustness over-claim. Round 4 verified clean-directory reproducibility. Round 5 corrected false \"15/15 PASS\" claim and documented the angular coefficient reproducibility gap.", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_37c858ca6f224bd9a2844af6"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:15.496051+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:16.984479+00:00"}}

