id: 2179
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 2179, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "0c4257af-a6cd-46cd-9653-984a5289ce34", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "tool", "position": 2175, "revision": 2179, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"offset\": 85}", "output": "85\t## Round 4: Clean-directory reproduction verification\n86\t- Executed `working/reproduce_clean_v2.py` to rebuild all artifacts from raw data into `reproduce_test/output/`\n87\t- Procedure: copy each script → patch OUT path → run sequentially from `data/` only → compare with authoritative `output/`\n88\t- Tolerance: 1e-6 absolute difference (deterministic algorithms: cubic spline, linregress, seeded noise)\n89\t- **Initial Result: 15/15 PASS** — but this was misleading because `independent_angular_coeff_results.json` in authoritative `output/` contained stale sub-agent output with wrong column mapping (index_1=2 instead of index_1=3 for F20). The clean-directory reproduction compared the same wrong file against itself.\n90\t- Full comparison: `reproduce_test/comparison_results.json`\n91\t- Caveat: `independent_angular_coeff_agent.py` has a column-parsing bug (reads wrong index_1 values); the authoritative result was copied from the incorrect Round 2 sub-agent output.\n92\t\n93\t## Round 5: Angular coefficient reproducibility gap resolved\n94\t- **Problem:** The authoritative `output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json` contained incorrect data from the original sub-agent (wrong column mapping: index_1=2 instead of index_1=3 for F20). The clean-directory \"15/15 PASS\" claim was false — it compared the wrong authoritative file against a reproduced version of the same wrong file.\n95\t- **Investigation:** Delegated sub-agent (a85d91b2fb09d939a) to rebuild from scratch. Sub-agent also selected index_1=2, producing wrong F20 values (0.003–0.005 range vs correct 0.26–1.44 range). Both the main-agent's representative reconstruction (`independent_angular_coeff_agent.py`) AND the sub-agent have the same column-parsing bug.\n96\t- **Resolution:** Main agent directly computed the correct results from raw data using proper column mapping (index_1=3 for F20 at both order=0 and order=1). Results written to both `output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json` and `reproduce_test/output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json`.\n97\t- **Corrected F20 values:** min=0.262@48.4 eV, max=1.435@27.9 eV, 6 extrema, order=1 sign changes=3.\n98\t- **Reproduction status:** 14/15 artifacts independently rebuilt via scripts and match within tolerance. 1 artifact (`independent_angular_coeff_results.json`) DIRECT_REBUILT — numerically identical but not independently rebuilt through a separate script.\n99\t- **Result.md updated:** Removed false \"All 15 core artifacts reproduce identically\" statement; added NOT_REBUILT/DIRECT_REBUILT entry with honest documentation of the column-parsing bug and its impact.\n100\t- **Validator passes:** 4 findings, 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n101\t", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_4bdfdecccc6e4a32b9f02c0f"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:27.303013+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:28.141033+00:00"}}

