data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 2197, "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "data": {"id": "a4eae622-22b7-4cf4-b41a-05cd3de7def1", "run_id": "run_a3995bac559c4563", "kind": "agent", "position": 1793, "revision": 2197, "parent_tool_use_id": "call_e7e057924f3a40a980c8d2d2", "agent_call_id": "b3ffe44d-6be1-4f63-8a26-cdae502c8404", "data": {"status": "completed", "agent_type": "general-purpose", "sdk_agent_id": "a85d91b2fb09d939a", "task": "You are a general-purpose sub-agent working on a scientific data analysis task. Your job is to independently recompute angular coefficient statistics from raw TSV data and save results to a specific output path.\n\n**Task:** Recompute Legendre angular coefficient F20 evolution from raw data, writing your own code from scratch (do NOT read or copy any existing analysis scripts). Save results to `[workspace]`.\n\n**Data file:** `[workspace]`\n\n**Data format:** Long-format TSV with columns: dataset_path, index_0, index_1, value. \n- Each energy block has a dataset_path like \"CoefLeg_22.5eV\", \"CoefLeg_23.25eV\", etc.\n- index_0 = 0 means order=0 coefficients; other values mean different orders.\n- The 13 measured energies are: 22.5, 23.25, 24.8, 26.35, 27.9, 29.45, 31.0, 32.55, 34.1, 35.65, 37.2, 38.75, 48.4 eV.\n- You need to extract F20 values at both order=0 and order=1 across all 13 energies.\n\n**What to compute and save as JSON:**\n```json\n{\n  \"analysis\": \"B - Angular Coefficient F20 Evolution (Independent Rebuild)\",\n  \"num_energy_levels\": 13,\n  \"energy_range_eV\": [22.5, 48.4],\n  \"f20_order0\": {\n    \"values\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>}, ...],\n    \"sequence\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"first_differences\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"local_extrema\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>, \"type\": \"min\"/\"max\"}, ...],\n    \"is_monotonic\": <bool>,\n    \"polynomial_fits\": {\"degree_3\": {\"coefficients\": [<float>,...], \"r_squared\": <float>}}\n  },\n  \"f20_order1\": {\n    \"values\": [{\"energy_eV\": <float>, \"F20_value\": <float>}, ...],\n    \"sequence\": [<float>, ...],\n    \"sign_changes\": <int>,\n    \"sign_change_energies\": []\n  },\n  \"all_order0_coeffs\": { \"<energy>\": { \"<index_1>\": <value>, ... }, ... },\n  \"all_order1_coeffs\": { \"<energy>\": { \"<index_1>\": <value>, ... }, ... }\n}\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Write your OWN code. Do not read any existing analysis scripts.\n- Use pandas/numpy/scipy only.\n- Be careful with column indexing — inspect the actual data structure first.\n- Save ONLY to the reproduce_test/output path specified above.\n- Print summary stats to stdout so I can verify.", "text": "The output file has been successfully written to `[workspace]`.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- **F20** (Legendre l=2 coefficient, `index_1=2`) was extracted from all 13 energy levels at both order=0 and order=1.\n- **Order 0 F20 values** range from 0.002577 (at 26.35 eV) to 0.005593 (at 34.1 eV). The sequence is non-monotonic with 7 local extrema (3 maxima, 4 minima). A degree-3 polynomial fit yields R-squared of 0.486, indicating moderate but not strong polynomial trend.\n- **Order 1 F20 values** range from 0.004463 (at 26.35 eV) to 0.009688 (at 34.1 eV). No sign changes were detected -- all values are positive across the full energy range.\n- All 13 energy coefficients (order=0 and order=1, indices 0-10) are stored in `all_order0_coeffs` and `all_order1_coeffs`.", "error_code": null}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:58:55.867396+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T10:04:35.455423+00:00"}}

